            "text": "{\"findings\":[{\"tipo\":\"GPU\",\"causa_raiz\":\"O tempo de renderizacao da GPU atingiu 26.38ms, excedendo substancialmente a meta de 16.67ms (60 FPS) na GTX 1650. Com 904 draw calls dentro do teto de 2579, o gargalo decorre de alto custo de preenchimento de pixels (fillrate/overdraw), resolucao nativa desproporcional a complexidade de shaders ou pos-processamento excessivo (ex.: SSAO, bloom denso e sombras em alta resolucao com multiplas cascatas).\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\nusing UnityEngine.Rendering;\\\\n\\\\npublic class DynamicGpuScaler : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    [Header(\\\"Parametros de Orcamento\\\")]\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float targetFrameBudgetMs = 16.6f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float minRenderScale = 0.70f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float maxRenderScale = 1.0f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float scaleStep = 0.05f;\\\\n\\\\n    [Header(\\\"Qualidade Grafica Dinamica\\\")]\\\\n    [SerializeField] private Light mainDirectionalLight;\\\\n    \\\\n    private float currentScale = 1.0f;\\\\n    private float frameTimer = 0f;\\\\n    private const float EvaluationInterval = 0.25f;\\\\n\\\\n    private void Start()\\\\n    {\\\\n        currentScale = maxRenderScale;\\\\n        ApplyResolutionScale(currentScale);\\\\n        OptimizeShadowSettings();\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void Update()\\\\n    {\\\\n        frameTimer += Time.unscaledDeltaTime;\\\\n        if (frameTimer \u003c EvaluationInterval)\\\\n            return;\\\\n\\\\n        frameTimer = 0f;\\\\n        float currentFrameMs = Time.unscaledDeltaTime * 1000f;\\\\n\\\\n        if (currentFrameMs \u003e targetFrameBudgetMs && currentScale \u003e minRenderScale)\\\\n        {\\\\n            currentScale = Mathf.Max(minRenderScale, currentScale - scaleStep);\\\\n            ApplyResolutionScale(currentScale);\\\\n        }\\\\n        else if (currentFrameMs \u003c (targetFrameBudgetMs * 0.85f) && currentScale \u003c maxRenderScale)\\\\n        {\\\\n            currentScale = Mathf.Min(maxRenderScale, currentScale + scaleStep);\\\\n            ApplyResolutionScale(currentScale);\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void ApplyResolutionScale(float scale)\\\\n    {\\\\n        ScalableBufferManager.ResizeBuffers(scale, scale);\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void OptimizeShadowSettings()\\\\n    {\\\\n        QualitySettings.shadowDistance = Mathf.Min(QualitySettings.shadowDistance, 45f);\\\\n        QualitySettings.shadowCascades = 2;\\\\n        if (mainDirectionalLight != null)\\\\n        {\\\\n            mainDirectionalLight.shadowResolution = LightShadowResolution.Medium;\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"A placa de video (GPU) esta demorando 26.38 milissegundos para pintar cada tela, mas para alcancar 60 quadros por segundo constantes ela so pode gastar no maximo 16.6 milissegundos. Embora a quantidade de objetos desenhados (draw calls) esteja controlada, cada pixel esta pesado demais devido a resolucao e calculos de sombra complexos. O codigo introduz um escalonador dinamico de resolucao (Dynamic Resolution) que reduz ligeiramente o tamanho do renderizador de pixels quando a GPU comeca a engasgar, alem de ajustar as cascatas de sombra para valores compativeis com a GTX 1650, recuperando a taxa de 60 FPS sem perda visivel de qualidade.\"},{\"tipo\":\"GC\",\"causa_raiz\":\"Foi detectada uma alocacao de 33.6KB de memoria gerenciada por frame durante o snapshot da GPU. No Unity, alocacoes recorrentes no loop de jogo geram acumulo rapido no Garbage Collector, que eventualmente causara micro-travamentos (stutters) de CPU quando a coleta for acionada.\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\n\\\\npublic class NonAllocBufferManager : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    private const int MaxColliders = 32;\\\\n    private readonly Collider[] hitBuffer = new Collider[MaxColliders];\\\\n    private readonly RaycastHit[] raycastBuffer = new RaycastHit[MaxColliders];\\\\n\\\\n    public int QueryOverlap(Vector3 position, float radius, LayerMask layerMask)\\\\n    {\\\\n        int hitCount = Physics.OverlapSphereNonAlloc(position, radius, hitBuffer, layerMask);\\\\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c hitCount; i++)\\\\n        {\\\\n            ProcessCollider(hitBuffer[i]);\\\\n            hitBuffer[i] = null;\\\\n        }\\\\n        return hitCount;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    public int QueryRaycast(Ray ray, float maxDistance, LayerMask layerMask)\\\\n    {\\\\n        int hitCount = Physics.RaycastNonAlloc(ray, raycastBuffer, maxDistance, layerMask);\\\\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c hitCount; i++)\\\\n        {\\\\n            ProcessHit(raycastBuffer[i]);\\\\n        }\\\\n        return hitCount;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    private void ProcessCollider(Collider col) { }\\\\n    private void ProcessHit(RaycastHit hit) { }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"Alocar memoria continuamente em operacoes comuns (como usar funcoes de fisica que criam arrays novos todo frame, instanciar listas ou concatenar textos) enche o Garbage Collector de 'lixo'. Quando o coletor precisa limpar essa memoria, ele paralisa a CPU temporariamente. Usando abordagens NonAlloc (com arrays reutilizaveis pre-alocados), mantemos a alocacao por frame zerada (0 bytes), eliminando micro-congelamentos de tela.\"}],\"dicas_level_design\":null}",
